# PageFlip force-sync test, RIGHT half (slot 1) -- the device being pushed to (section 5.1).
#
# Started with a different screen margin, so it reports the mismatch exactly as the negative pair
# test does. The difference is what happens next: the left half confirms, this half preflights the
# offer, answers it, and applies the commit -- and nothing is written before that answer.
#
# Receives no input of its own. Its own prompt is dismissed by the arriving offer, because the
# choice of source is made the moment either user confirms.
log pageflip-fs-right: start
expect_timeout 60000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
wait 9000
expect incompatible layout
screenshot /screenshots/pf-fs-right-00.bmp
# The preflight runs on the offer and writes nothing; the verdict is what the source commits on.
expect PageFlip settings preflight
expect PageFlip applied the pair's settings
# The rebuild re-lays out the chapter at the new margin, and the re-greet that follows is what
# proves the two devices finally agree.
wait 12000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-fs-right-01.bmp
wait 2000
log pageflip-fs-right: done
quit
